      "blockId": "paragraph:discussion:0009",
      "type": "sentence",
      "source": "If you set this property’s value to `1.0`, this denoiser scaler expects that each pixel’s motion vector points to that pixel’s location in the [`colorTexture`](mtlfxtemporaldenoisedscalerbase/colortexture.md) at the time of the last call to encode this scaler’s work.",
      "normalizedSource": "If you set this property’s value to `1.0`, this denoiser scaler expects that each pixel’s motion vector points to that pixel’s location in the [`colorTexture`](mtlfxtemporaldenoisedscalerbase/colortexture.md) at the time of the last call to encode this scaler’s work.",
      "sourceHash": "abd5515722aa6617de0db5a62929b08d1f38190a1263278050d77034fedcb055",
      "translatable": true,
      "contextBefore": "The scaler converts the horizontal component of each value in [`motionTexture`](mtlfxtemporaldenoisedscalerbase/motiontexture.md) into fragment (pixel) coordinates by multiplying it by this property’s value.",
      "contextAfter": "For example, in Metal’s standard device coordinates, where `(0,0)` represents the upper-left corner of the framebuffer, the motion vectors for an object that moves down and to the right in the [`colorTexture`](mtlfxtemporaldenoisedscalerbase/colortexture.md) by `10` pixels would be `(-10,-10)`.",
